Keep mkswap in the otherwise libraries-only build.

util-linux 2.40.2 exposes --enable-swapon, but no --enable-mkswap. Its
UL_BUILD_INIT([mkswap], [yes]) unconditionally inherits --disable-all-programs,
even if enable_mkswap was supplied by the caller. systemd-repart needs the real
mkswap executable to initialise Format=swap; systemd does not replace it.

Change the shipped configure directly so this does not introduce an autoconf
dependency on the build host. This intentionally makes mkswap the one exception
to --disable-all-programs; all other programs retain their upstream selection.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -36135,7 +36135,7 @@
   enable_mkswap=$ul_default_estate
   build_mkswap=yes
   if test "x$ul_default_estate" = xno; then
-    build_mkswap=no
+    build_mkswap=yes
   fi
 else
 
